[Event "Scandinavian: 3.Nc3 Qa5 Main Line"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 {The Scandinavian: attack e4 right away!} 2. exd5 Qxd5 {Take back with the queen.} 3. Nc3 Qa5 {The queen is safe on a5 and pins the knight.} 4. d4 Nf6 {Develop.} 5. Nf3 c6 {Make a safe square on c7 for your queen.} 6. Bc4 Bf5 {The bishop comes out before ...e6.} 7. Bd2 e6 {Now your pawns are like a wall.} 8. Qe2 Bb4 {Pin the knight.} 9. O-O-O Nbd7 10. a3 Bxc3 11. Bxc3 Qc7 {Your queen is safe. Castle next.} *

[Event "Scandinavian: 3.Nc3 Qa5 4.Nf3"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. d4 Bf5 {Bishop out first.} 6. Bc4 e6 7. Bd2 c6 8. Nd5 {White attacks the queen.} Qd8 {The queen goes home – that is fine.} 9. Nxf6+ Qxf6 {Take back with the queen. Solid.} 10. Qe2 Bd6 *

[Event "Scandinavian: 3.Nc3 Qd6"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qd6 {Another safe square for the queen.} 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 a6 {Stop Nb5, which would attack your queen.} 6. g3 Bg4 {Develop with a pin.} 7. Bg2 Nc6 8. O-O O-O-O {Castle long and attack d4.} *

[Event "Scandinavian: 3.Nf3"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nf3 {White doesn't chase your queen.} Nf6 4. d4 Bf5 {Bishop out before ...e6.} 5. Be2 e6 6. O-O c6 {A solid wall of pawns.} 7. c4 Qd8 {The queen goes home, safe from attacks.} 8. Nc3 Be7 {Castle next. Solid and safe.} *

[Event "Scandinavian: 3.d4"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. d4 {White takes the center.} Nf6 4. Nf3 Bg4 {Pin the knight.} 5. Be2 e6 6. O-O Nc6 7. c4 Qd7 {The queen steps back but stays active.} 8. Nc3 O-O-O {Castle long – your rook and queen hit d4.} *

[Event "Scandinavian: 2.e5"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. e5 {White doesn't take.} Bf5 {Your bishop comes out before ...e6.} 3. d4 e6 4. Nf3 c5 {Attack White's pawn chain from the side.} 5. c3 Nc6 6. Be2 Qb6 {Pressure on d4 and b2.} 7. O-O cxd4 {Open the c-file.} 8. cxd4 Nge7 {The knight goes to f5 and hits d4 again.} *

[Event "Scandinavian: 2.Nc3"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. Nc3 {White protects e4.} d4 {Kick the knight away!} 3. Nce2 e5 {Take space in the center.} 4. Ng3 Be6 {Develop and guard the light squares.} 5. Nf3 f6 {Hold e5 strongly.} 6. Bb5+ c6 7. Ba4 Nd7 *

[Event "Scandinavian: 2...Nf6"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 {Don't hurry – take the pawn back with the knight.} 3. d4 Nxd5 4. Nf3 g6 {Your bishop will be strong on g7.} 5. Be2 Bg7 6. O-O O-O {Safe king, then fight for the center.} 7. c4 Nb6 8. Nc3 Bg4 {Pressure on d4.} *

[Event "Scandinavian: Blackmar-Diemer Gambit 2.d4"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. d4 {The Blackmar-Diemer Gambit: White offers a pawn for a fast attack.} dxe4 {Take it.} 3. Nc3 Nf6 {Protect e4 and develop.} 4. f3 exf3 {Take again – now White has an open f-file but you are a pawn up.} 5. Nxf3 Bg4 {Pin the knight.} 6. h3 Bxf3 7. Qxf3 c6 {Close the long diagonal to b7.} 8. Be3 e6 {A solid wall. Next ...Nbd7 and ...Be7.} 9. Bd3 Nbd7 10. O-O Be7 *

[Event "Scandinavian: 3.Nc3 Qa5 4.Bc4"]
[Opening "Scandinavian"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. Bc4 {The bishop aims at f7.} Nf6 5. d3 c6 {Give your queen a way back to c7.} 6. Bd2 Qc7 {Out of the pin line – no tricks with Nd5 or Nb5.} 7. Nf3 Bg4 {Pin the knight.} 8. h3 Bh5 9. Qe2 e6 *
